Counterfactual for borg-reborn-rs#929 (applied to borg-core at 4b2c2fcf, built, never committed).
With CF929 set in the environment, borg_target_unknown_wall never writes the guessed wall on the
Borg's own grid: the walk skips that grid, and the "pathway found the target" branch returns false
(no guess, successful_target stays negative) when the step back lands on the Borg.
--- a/borg-core/src/borg_projection.rs
+++ b/borg-core/src/borg_projection.rs
@@
-        if feat_is(st.cave.grid(n_x, n_y), FEAT_NONE)
+        if std::env::var_os("CF929").is_some() && n_x == st.borg.c.x && n_y == st.borg.c.y && !(n_x == x && n_y == y) {
+            // counterfactual (#929): skip the Borg's own grid
+        } else if feat_is(st.cave.grid(n_x, n_y), FEAT_NONE)
             && (n_y != st.borg.c.y || !y_hall)
@@
